 {"id":"C30","title":"Kabir reads the candles","text":"Kabir watches Alpha Ltd. After falling for six sessions, Alpha forms a candle with a small body near the day's high and a lower shadow three times the body. Months later, near the top of a long trading range, a strong green candle is followed by a candle that opens with a gap up but closes red, below the midpoint of the green candle.",
  "qs":[
   {"q":"The candle after the six-session fall is most likely a:","o":["Hammer","Hanging man","Evening star","Dark cloud cover"],"a":0,"w":"Small body, long lower shadow at least twice the body, after a decline."},
   {"q":"What does Kabir need before acting on it?","o":["Confirmation: price must start moving up next","Nothing; act immediately","A gap down the next day","RSI above 70"],"a":0,"w":"The book says trades are typically taken after the confirmation candle."},
   {"q":"The gap-up red candle closing below the green candle's midpoint, at the top of a range, is:","o":["Dark cloud cover","Piercing pattern","Morning star","Bullish engulfing"],"a":0,"w":"A bearish two-candle pattern near the top of a congestion area."},
   {"q":"If the same shape as the first candle had appeared after a strong rise, it would be a:","o":["Hanging man, a bearish warning","Hammer, bullish","Bullish engulfing","Morning star"],"a":0,"w":"The hanging man needs the next candle to close lower to confirm."},
  ]},
